<title>FINLAND: MERITA TO AUCTION OWN 2001-BOND JAN 16.</title>
<headline>MERITA TO AUCTION OWN 2001-BOND JAN 16.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-01-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish commercial bank Merita Pankki, part of banking group Merita Oy said in a statement on Thursday it will auction on January 16 its own bonds carrying a 5.5-percent coupon and maturing in 2001.</p>
<p>In the first auction of the bonds in November, Merita sold 353 million markka worth of paper. The issue price was 99.854 and the yield was 5.53 percent.</p>
<p>On Thursday afternoon, Finnish government 2001 bonds yielded 4.90 percent.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
</text>
